- op: discuss  # 51a5
  at: '2026-11-09T11:13:28Z'  # 51a5
  by: agent  # 51a5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 51a5
  clock: 3  # 51a5
  nonce: 51a5  # 51a5
  message: "Fixed in PR #2103. Two causes: the same-file branch bound the bare short name (last declaration wins), and the resolver indexes methods under bare names too, returning an 'exact' hit for Other.helper, with no INV-fahub guard on Kotlin's simple-call path at all. Now: prefer Enclosing.callee; a short-name hit on another type's method goes through defer_bare_method_call('suffix'); the resolver branch reads an 'exact' hit whose name differs from the callee as short-name evidence unless an import names the callee (test_jvm_import_outranks_project_name caught the okhttp Companion import case before push). Withheld calls are unresolved with enclosing_class for the inherited-calls linker. Live repro, dev vs branch: Point { m() = helper() } + Other { helper() } in one file and in two files -> dev Point.m -> Other.helper, branch unresolved helper with enclosing_class Point; nested Inner.m -> Inner.h, companion Outer.useC -> Outer.c and free caller -> top unchanged. Known cost, shown by the same repro: o.run { helper() } bound to Other.helper on dev (right by accident) and is unresolved on the branch, since scope-function receivers are not typed."  # 51a5
